{
  "correction_rules": [
    "Persistent low bias: model forecasts are systematically below realized prices by ~+1 to +3 EUR for most of the first ~20 forecast days (strongest during uptrends). Apply an upward level-shift to the whole path, especially early horizon.",
    "Trend/acceleration underestimation: when the recent 30d history is rising, the model lags and fails to capture the subsequent rally (true series steps up into ~68–70 while model stays ~65–67). Add a momentum/acceleration term tied to the last 5–10 day slope.",
    "Late-horizon overshoot: beyond ~day 20 the model often projects excessive upside (spikes to ~70–72) while the true path flattens or reverses. Dampen long-horizon trend extrapolation; cap upside drift and increase mean-reversion strength after day ~20.",
    "Poor turning-point timing: model peaks occur later/higher than realized (predicts continued rise while true begins to roll over). Introduce a regime switch: after a strong run-up, increase probability/weight of consolidation/pullback in weeks 3–4.",
    "Volatility misallocation: model produces sharper late spikes than observed, while missing earlier step-changes. Smooth late-horizon volatility and shift some variance to earlier horizons (faster adjustment to new levels, less explosive tails later)."
  ]
}
